{"type":"text","timestamp":"2026-10-10T22:14:40.190Z","data":{"text":"All verifies pass, and every file I changed is inside the task's scope (plus the result file). \n\n## Summary\n\n**Task**: When the validator runs on another harness, `osq doctor` checks that harness's binary and version as it checks the executor's.\n\n**Changes**:\n1. **`src/core/foundation/doctor-validator.ts`** — Added `checkValidatorHarness` (with `HarnessProbe` type), which:\n   - returns no checks when the validator is disabled/absent or its harness equals the executor's (normalized comparison);\n   - builds the validator's run config via `validatorRunConfig(config, validator)`;\n   - runs the shared probe on it, renaming the result to `validator-harness`;\n   - after a passing probe, appends the harness catalog's `diagnose` checks with their names prefixed `validator-`, carrying the warning flag.\n   - Carries `@scenario cli-foundation:` tags for the four scenarios and `@adr 010`.\n\n2. **`src/core/foundation/doctor.ts`** — `runDoctorChecks` now pushes those checks right before `validator-model` (after `planning-prices`), reusing the existing `checkHarness` probe passed as a value rather than writing a second one. File stays at 249 counted lines (≤ 250).\n\n3. **`tests/validator-doctor-harness.test.ts`** — New plain `node:test` file proving all four scenarios with the fake Claude binary (`OSQ_FAKE_CLAUDE_VERSION`, saved/restored as `exec-doctor.test.ts` does), executor harness `mock`, through `runDoctorChecks` with `loadConfig`/`probeValidator` injected.\n\n**Verification**: Task verify passes (4/4 tests); `tests/validator-doctor.test.ts` (6/6) and `tests/doctor.test.ts` (28/28, including the own-repo check that probes the installed `claude` 2.1.278) pass unchanged; the proposal's `pnpm verify` exits 0."}}
